{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "recorded_at": "2026-09-17T17:07:26.818Z",
  "launch_context": "Claude Code on the web (remote sandbox), signed-in claude CLI, organisation egress policy through an agent proxy; not the keeper's native machine. Codex CLI is not installed here.",
  "what_this_is": "Two live host capability probes for the Claude host under the frozen schema-4 plan and the unchanged September 17 allowlist (curl, node). A probe qualifies a host and adapter; it is not a buyer journey and names no service.",
  "result": "Both probes pass: the host retained the public bytes exactly and verified the runner-minted ed25519 vectors with node crypto (SPKI-wrapped raw key) — the permitted path neither September 17 Claude buyer attempted.",
  "first_probe_defect": "The first probe used one shared message, so with deterministic ed25519 the two valid signatures were identical bytes and the two tampered ones were identical; the host noticed. The instrument now mints one message per vector; the second probe ran on the corrected instrument (see instrument_sha256). The first probe is retained, not rescored.",
  "observations": [
    "Refusals in this launch context were compound commands (semicolon- or newline-separated) and a heredoc redirect; a curl chained with && to echo, and plain ls/echo/cat-free commands, ran. The host's own attribution of the first refusal to curl flag order is contradicted by the trace, which shows the refused commands were the compound ones.",
    "Commands not on the allowlist (ls, echo) executed in dontAsk mode; the allowlist is not the only allow path in this Claude Code version. Recorded, not relied on.",
    "The second probe's host self-report listed no refused commands while the trace shows one refused cat heredoc; self-reports are statements, the trace is the record.",
    "The merchant subject https://lionx402.com is refused by this sandbox's egress policy (CONNECT 403), so the buyer cohort was not run here; scvd.store, raw.githubusercontent.com and the MCP registry are reachable."
  ],
  "cohort_run": false,
  "private_originals": "Raw traces, retained files, launch metadata and reference bytes stay under the ignored private/ directory and were handed to the keeper as an archive; this record lists every file with its hash.",
